CanonicalBridge::constructor
├── it sets the owner with DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE
├── it grants PAUSER_ROLE to the owner
├── it grants STARTER_ROLE to the owner
├── it grants WITHDRAWAL_AUTHORITY_ROLE to the owner
├── it grants WITHDRAWAL_CANCELLER_ROLE to the owner
├── it grants FRAUD_WINDOW_SETTER_ROLE to the owner
├── it sets the TREASURY address
├── it sets the MAILBOX address
├── it emits a Deployed event
└── it sets the default fraud window duration

CanonicalBridge::deposit
├── when the contract is paused
│   └── it reverts
├── when the recipient is not initialized
│   └── it reverts
├── when the deposit amount does not match ETH sent
│   └── it reverts with DepositAmountMismatch
├── when the deposit amount is not divisible by WEI_PER_LAMPORT
│   └── it reverts with FractionalValueNotAllowed
├── when the deposit amount is less than MIN_DEPOSIT
│   └── it reverts with DepositLessThanMinimum
├── when the transfer to TREASURY fails
│   └── it reverts with TransferFailed
└── when all deposit conditions are met
    ├── it transfers the deposit to the TREASURY
    ├── it sends a deposit message to the MAILBOX
    └── it emits a Deposited event

CanonicalBridge::authorizeWithdrawals
├── when the contract is paused for authorizeWithdrawals
│   └── it reverts
├── when the caller is not WITHDRAWAL_AUTHORITY_ROLE for authorizeWithdrawals
│   └── it reverts with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount
└── when all authorizeWithdrawals conditions are met
    ├── it decodes the messages
    └── it calls _authorizeWithdrawal for each message

CanonicalBridge::authorizeWithdrawal
├── when the contract is paused for authorizeWithdrawal
│   └── it reverts
├── when the caller is not WITHDRAWAL_AUTHORITY_ROLE for authorizeWithdrawal
│   └── it reverts with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount
└── when all authorizeWithdrawal conditions are met
    ├── it decodes the message
    └── it calls _authorizeWithdrawal for the message

CanonicalBridge::claimWithdrawal
├── when the contract is paused for claimWithdrawal
│   └── it reverts
├── when the withdrawal is not authorized
│   └── it reverts with WithdrawalUnauthorized
├── when the withdrawal fails
│   └── it reverts with WithdrawalFailed
└── when all claimWithdrawal conditions are met
    ├── it transfers funds to the recipient
    ├── it transfers the fee to the fee receiver
    ├── it marks the withdrawal as claimed
    └── it emits a WithdrawalClaimed event

CanonicalBridge::deleteWithdrawMessage
├── when called with a message
│   ├── when the caller is not WITHDRAWAL_CANCELLER_ROLE for message deletion
│   │   └── it reverts with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount
│   ├── when the withdraw message is invalid
│   │   └── it reverts with InvalidWithdrawMessage
│   └── when all message deletion conditions are met
│       ├── it deletes the withdraw message
│       └── it emits a WithdrawMessageDeleted event
└── when called with a hash
    ├── when the caller is not WITHDRAWAL_CANCELLER_ROLE for hash deletion
    │   └── it reverts with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount
    ├── when the withdrawal status is not PENDING
    │   └── it reverts with CannotCancel
    └── when all hash deletion conditions are met
        ├── it deletes the withdraw message
        └── it emits a WithdrawMessageHashDeleted event

CanonicalBridge::setFraudWindowDuration
├── when the caller is not FRAUD_WINDOW_SETTER_ROLE
│   └── it reverts with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount
├── when the duration is less than MIN_fraudWindowDuration
│   └── it reverts with DurationTooShort
└── when all setFraudWindowDuration conditions are met
    ├── it sets the new fraud window duration
    └── it emits a FraudWindowSet event

CanonicalBridge::pause
├── when the caller is not PAUSER_ROLE
│   └── it reverts with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount
└── when the caller has PAUSER_ROLE
    ├── it pauses the contract
    └── it emits a Paused event

CanonicalBridge::unpause
├── when the caller is not STARTER_ROLE
│   └── it reverts with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount
└── when the caller has STARTER_ROLE
    ├── it unpauses the contract
    └── it emits an Unpaused event

CanonicalBridge::withdrawMessageStatus
├── when called with a message
│   ├── when the withdraw message is invalid for status check
│   │   └── it reverts with InvalidWithdrawMessage
│   └── when the message is valid for status check
│       └── it returns the correct withdrawal status
└── when called with a hash
    ├── when the message is unknown
    │   └── it returns WithdrawStatus.UNKNOWN
    ├── when the message is closed
    │   └── it returns WithdrawStatus.CLOSED
    └── when the message is pending
        └── it returns WithdrawStatus.PENDING

CanonicalBridge::withdrawMessageHash
└── it returns the correct hash of the withdraw message

CanonicalBridge::getVersionComponents
└── it returns the correct version numbers